  "notes": [
    "Structural estimates from EIA Table 1 and the tabulated LNG series in Tables 2–6 and 8. Oil means crude oil, condensate and petroleum products. Volumes are daily averages and are reported at EIA's precision.",
    "Panama oil values are fiscal-year averages. Table 7 identifies the overview's final Panama figure as FY 2025 (October 2024 through September 2025). This is the sole series whose final period extends beyond June 2025. Panama canal oil excludes the Trans-Panama Pipeline.",
    "Panama LNG is omitted because the report gives only an approximate FY 2021 figure and an upper bound for FY 2025 in prose, with no comparable tabulated series.",
    "Suez oil covers the canal and SUMED Pipeline together. Suez LNG covers the canal only.",
    "Danish Straits oil excludes Kiel Canal flows. The source reports the Danish Straits together, so the values apply to the grouped route rather than to any one strait.",
    "The Turkish Straits series in Table 1 uses Dardanelles oil. LNG also uses the Dardanelles. The separate Bosporus oil series is outside the Table 1 scope.",
    "EIA describes the Bab el-Mandeb LNG values displayed as 0.0 in 2024 and the first half of 2025 as near zero.",
    "The Cape of Good Hope is an alternative sea route. Individual route volumes can overlap where shipments traverse multiple locations. The world maritime oil trade and world total oil supply rows are global comparators and are excluded.",
    "The route IDs identify EIA scopes for this hand table. Live traffic IDs require a separate mapping and may cover different geographic scopes.",
    "The table includes only EIA's published aggregates. EIA drew on Vortexa tracking, Panama Canal Authority data and the February 2026 Short-Term Energy Outlook."
  ],
